  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 413 AM MDT THU OCT 22 2026\nShort-lived upper-level ridging will build in Sunday as the \narea is between a closed low in the Four Corners and another\nsystem moving into the Pacific NW. This will enable dry \nconditions and a slight warming trend through Monday, causing\ntemperatures to climb to about 5 degrees above normal Sunday \nand Monday. Cooler and wetter conditions are expected to return \nduring the mid week as the upper-level trough moves further \ninland and overhead. Lingering forecast uncertainty exists for \nthe timing and track of this low pressure system, with \ndisagreement present in ensemble solutions and between \ndeterministic models. Current forecast shows this cut off low \nbringing much cooler, below normal temperatures and 20-40% \nchances of precipitation over the higher terrain of eastern \nOregon and west-central Idaho. Snow levels will likely range \nfrom 5500-6500 ft MSL, depending on the track of the low \npressure, with light mountain snow accumulation.",
